# XSH calloc()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.calloc.001
anchor     functions/calloc.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Space from calloc() is all bits zero: after a block is dirtied
           (malloc, fill with a non-zero byte, free), calloc() blocks of the
           same and other sizes read back as all zero bytes.
test       t/001-zero-filled.c

assertion  XSH.calloc.002
anchor     functions/calloc.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/calloc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       calloc(n, s) returns a non-null, fundamentally aligned pointer to
           n*s usable bytes, and live results are pairwise disjoint.
test       t/002-array.c

assertion  XSH.calloc.003
anchor     functions/calloc.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       calloc() with nelem or elsize 0 returns either a null pointer or a
           freeable pointer, and two non-null live results differ.
test       t/003-zero-size.c

assertion  XSH.calloc.004
anchor     functions/calloc.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      2024
says       When nelem * elsize would overflow size_t, calloc() returns a null
           pointer and sets errno to ENOMEM.
test       t/004-overflow.c

assertion  XSH.calloc.005
anchor     functions/calloc.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/calloc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       calloc(1, SIZE_MAX) (no overflow, impossible to satisfy) returns a
           null pointer and sets errno to ENOMEM.
test       t/005-failure.c
